WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.810
Once authentication has moved,
a different question opens up:

2
00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.612
which platform should
each data domain live on?

3
00:00:06.612 --> 00:00:10.800
That choice isn't forced, so it
comes after, one domain at a time.

4
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.657
Stay on SQL Server, or move
to PostgreSQL or Oracle;

5
00:00:14.657 --> 00:00:17.813
each can support the identity requirement.

6
00:00:17.813 --> 00:00:22.691
The book scores them on ten dimensions
with evidence, from migration effort and

7
00:00:22.691 --> 00:00:24.761
skills to licensing and exit cost,

8
00:00:24.761 --> 00:00:28.087
and two domains reaching
different answers is normal.

9
00:00:28.087 --> 00:00:31.850
The goal is fewer authoritative
platforms, not one vendor.

10
00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:36.345
So the decision for the CIO and
data leadership: choose per domain,

11
00:00:36.345 --> 00:00:41.838
after closure, as its own funded decision,
with the same parallel-run discipline.

12
00:00:41.838 --> 00:00:43.750
Let's pull the decisions together.
